# {{MODEL}}

A Juno Cassandra **custom domain model**, scaffolded by `jcass-dm scaffold --from-sample`.

Unlike an empty scaffold, this one **runs**. It carries a small working model — generic assets
with an age, a condition and a material — so you can prove the whole pipeline before you write a
line of your own engineering: build it, upload it, debug it, publish it, run it.

**This is the model you keep.** There is no throwaway project and no rename later. You replace the
sample's logic with your own, one file at a time, with a working build at every step.

---

## 0. Where to run the commands on this page

**Every command here is typed into a PowerShell terminal sitting in the Assistant folder** — the
folder holding `tools\jcass-dm.exe`, next door to this one. In VS Code: **Terminal → New Terminal**,
then check with `pwd`.

That is why the commands say `.\tools\jcass-dm.exe` (the tool, in the folder you are in) and
`..\{{MODEL}}` (this project, next door). Run them from inside this folder instead and PowerShell
answers *"The term '.\tools\jcass-dm.exe' is not recognized"* — it is not there, and nothing is
wrong beyond which folder you are standing in.

The Assistant's `docs\orientation\running-commands.md` covers this in five minutes if any of it is
unfamiliar.

